      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Piascledine is a plant drug which positively influences the metabolism of cartilage and bone tissues. The authors studied the therapeutic effect of the drug in outpatients with chronic nonspecific dorsalgia. Piascledine was administered in dose 300 mg daily during two months. In the first month, it was used in the combination with artrosilene (320 mg daily). A comparison group included patients receiving monotherapy with NSAIDs (artrosilene). The study confirmed the high analgesic efficacy of piascledine in the treatment of patients with chronic nonspecific dorsalgia with controlled using of NSAIDs. The positive effect of piascledine was demonstrated after one month of treatment. The authors suggest that further clinical trials and placebo-control studies are needed to confirm these results."},
